(Bug #95. A format hole reads the slot as whatever type the name carries,
 so a text brought into being by an untyped declaration interpolated the
 address the integer formatter made of it - the same wrong answer `Print
 label.` gave, arriving through the other reader.)

Set label to "hello".
Print "the label is {label}".

the greeting is "good day".
Print "{greeting}, all".

Set tally to 5.
Print "tally {tally}".
